  "notes": "# DevClash 0.1.0-beta.10\n\nLower memory use when tracking large AI usage histories and syncing them to the cloud.\n\n- Avoid full-history copies during scanning, deduplication, daily aggregation and cloud preparation.\n- Read and save local metadata caches through bounded buffers.\n- Share repeated project metadata, including when growing logs are reparsed.\n- Skip already-synced usage before allocating upload records, while preserving complete Cursor snapshots and retries.\n- Preserve usage totals, duplicate detection, saved history, account login, sync consent and display preferences.\n\nControlled local benchmarks showed substantially lower peak memory. Actual memory use depends on the size of your history and current activity. This remains a beta; package and device evidence is recorded separately. Existing beta.9 installers remain unchanged.\n\nBuilt locally on native hosts. Source commit: 4441bc0ab11ed40647d6d01ca7f38eebc5d259a9.\n\nAvailability: Mac (Apple Silicon and Intel) and Linux (DEB and AppImage) receive beta.10. Windows remains on its existing signed beta.9 release; beta.10 Windows packaging is deferred.\n",
